1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,695
Two hundred suppliers reply to an RFQ.

2
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:06,123
PDFs, spreadsheets, prices buried in emails.

3
00:00:06,253 --> 00:00:08,276
Today, that's hours of manual entry.

4
00:00:08,876 --> 00:00:09,932
Now, one prompt.

5
00:00:10,382 --> 00:00:12,686
Claude reads the replies with read-only access,

6
00:00:12,761 --> 00:00:14,813
matches each one to its RFQ,

7
00:00:14,950 --> 00:00:16,683
fills our template to our rules,

8
00:00:16,756 --> 00:00:18,835
and checks every file before it's saved.

9
00:00:19,335 --> 00:00:20,827
You get a folder ready to import,

10
00:00:21,001 --> 00:00:22,089
and a report that flags

11
00:00:22,089 --> 00:00:23,178
what needs a human eye.

12
00:00:23,728 --> 00:00:24,775
Hours of data entry

13
00:00:24,775 --> 00:00:26,154
become minutes of review.

14
00:00:26,278 --> 00:00:28,120
Let's pilot it on one folio.

